# Scripts run under bash on Linux CI and under Git Bash on Windows. A CRLF
# checkout breaks both (`$'\r': command not found`), and a Windows machine with
# core.autocrlf=true would produce exactly that, so pin them to LF regardless.
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.py            text eol=lf
.claude/bin/*   text eol=lf

# Add your toolchain's generated files here if they are committed and the tool
# writes LF everywhere (e.g. Godot's `*.import`). Otherwise every test run on
# Windows leaves them "modified" with no content change and trips every
# clean-tree precondition.
